      "abstract": [
        "A polygon showing the permanent buildings or structures, including the building footprint. Attributes include the building types, building names, building height etc."
      ],
      "lineage": [
        "The building footprint is normally mapped using field survey, digitization from old survey sheets, conversion from building plans and/or photogrammetric techniques, delineating the ground-level outline of structures that are visible above-ground.\n\nAll entities within the Building Footprint sub theme are based on DAM Building CSU. The existing data exchange process of the DAM Building CSU will be kept, and the data conversion process was conducted to convert Building Data from DAM into the schema of the Building Footprint sub theme. A single unified building structure layer is formed by combining all spatial entities in Building CSU which are based on 1:1000 digital map data from LandsD. Textual building geographical and structural information provided by data owners of Building CSU (i.e. ArchSD, BD, LandsD, PlanD, RVD and HD) are also adopted."
      ],
      "use_limitations": [
        "Please note that the position accuracy of data varies from about 0.015m in the best to 1.500m to the worst."
      ],
      "height_coverage": {
        "base_and_top_positive_difference": 127,
        "missing_or_invalid_base_top": 291,
        "note": "Top/Base are datum heights; use TopHeight-BaseHeight, not TopHeight as extrusion."
      }
    },
